.\" Title: vrc
.\" Manual section: 1
.\"
.TH VRC 1 "2025" "vrc" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
vrc \- a virtual terminal runner

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vrc
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIARGS\fR...]
.br
.B vrc
\fBlist\fR [\fB\-\-target\fR \fIPID\fR] [\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interactive\fR]
.br
.B vrc
\fBstop\fR [\fIPID\fR] [\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interactive\fR]
.br
.B vrc
\fBkeys\fR \fIPID\fR [\fB\-c\fR \fIID\fR] \fIKEYS\fR
.br
.B vrc
\fBcat\fR \fIPID\fR [\fB\-c\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interactive\fR]
.br
.B vrc
\fBspawn\-in\fR \fIPID\fR \fICMD\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.br
.B vrc
\fBfreeze\fR \fIPID\fR [\fB\-c\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interactive\fR]
.br
.B vrc
\fBthaw\fR \fIPID\fR [\fB\-c\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interactive\fR]
.br
.B vrc
\fBresize\fR \fIPID\fR [\fB\-c\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-\-rows\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-cols\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interactive\fR]
.br
.B vrc
\fBkill\fR \fIPID\fR [\fB\-c\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-all\fR]
.br
.B vrc
\fBstop\-command\fR \fIPID\fR [\fB\-c\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-all\fR]
.br
.B vrc
\fBconfig\-check\fR
.br
.B vrc
\fBcompletions\fR \fISHELL\fR

.SH DESCRIPTION
vrc is a virtual terminal runner that manages pseudo-terminal (PTY) sessions for command-line programs. It runs commands in isolated VT100-compatible terminal emulators with full scrollback, allowing you to interact with them via the local terminal display or detach them to run in the background.

vrc uses Unix Domain Socket (UDS) IPC for inter-process communication. Running instances listen on control sockets at \fB~/.local/share/vrc/control\-{pid}.sock\fR, which CLI subcommands use to query state, send keystrokes, spawn additional commands, and manage running processes.

.SH COMMAND MODES

When a command is given (e.g., \fBvrc htop\fR), vrc spawns it inside a virtual terminal. By default, the command runs headlessly (no display). Use \fB\-\-display\fR to render the VTTY output in the local terminal.

.SS Instance Subcommands

These connect to already-running vrc instances via UDS:

.TP
.BR list " " [\fB\-\-target\fR \fIPID\fR] [\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interactive\fR]
List running instances and their commands. With \fB\-\-interactive\fR, presents a numbered list to select which instances to show.

.TP
.BR stop " " [\fIPID\fR] [\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interactive\fR]
Stop a running instance by sending SIGTERM. With \fB\-\-interactive\fR, presents a numbered list to select which instances to stop.

.TP
.BR keys " " \fIPID\fR [\fB\-c\fR \fIID\fR] \fIKEYS\fR
Send keystrokes to a command. Use \fB<Enter>\fR, \fB<C\-c>\fR, \fB<Esc>\fR, etc. for special keys.

.TP
.BR cat " " \fIPID\fR [\fB\-c\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interactive\fR]
Print the plain text output of a command's VTTY buffer. With \fB\-\-interactive\fR, presents a numbered list of commands to select.

.TP
.BR spawn\-in " " \fIPID\fR \fICMD\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
Spawn a new command inside a running instance.

.TP
.BR freeze " " \fIPID\fR [\fB\-c\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interactive\fR]
Suspend a command (SIGSTOP). With \fB\-\-interactive\fR, presents a numbered list to select which commands to freeze.

.TP
.BR thaw " " \fIPID\fR [\fB\-c\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interactive\fR]
Resume a suspended command (SIGCONT). With \fB\-\-interactive\fR, presents a numbered list to select which commands to thaw.

.TP
.BR resize " " \fIPID\fR [\fB\-c\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-\-rows N\fR] [\fB\-\-cols N\fR] [\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interactive\fR]
Resize a command's VTTY dimensions. With \fB\-\-interactive\fR, presents a numbered list to select which commands to resize.

.TP
.BR kill " " \fIPID\fR [\fB\-c\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-all\fR]
Kill a command inside an instance. With \fB\-\-interactive\fR, presents a numbered list to select which commands to kill. With \fB\-\-all\fR, stops all commands in the instance.

.TP
.BR stop\-command " " \fIPID\fR [\fB\-c\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-all\fR]
Stop a command (alias for kill). See \fBvrc\-kill\fR(1).

.TP
.BR config\-check
Validate configuration files without starting.

.TP
.BR completions " " \fISHELL\fR
Generate shell completion scripts.

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-display
Show VTTY output on the local terminal screen. Keeps displaying after the initial command exits (equivalent to the old \-\-display\-all).

.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemon
Run as a background daemon (Unix only).

.TP
.BR \-\-tabs
Show a tab bar for command switching in display mode.

.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Path to configuration file.

.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-profile " " \fINAME\fR
Apply a named configuration profile.

.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-working\-directory " " \fIDIR\fR
Set working directory for spawned commands.

.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-env " " \fIKEY=VALUE\fR
Set environment variables (repeatable).

.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-term " " \fITERM\fR
TERM value reported to child processes.

.TP
.BR \-\-vtty\-rows " " \fIN
VTTY rows.

.TP
.BR \-\-vtty\-cols " " \fIN
VTTY columns.

.TP
.BR \-\-scrollback " " \fIN
Scrollback buffer size (lines).

.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-retain\-on\-exit
Keep VTTY buffer after the command exits.

.TP
.BR \-\-snapshot\-on\-exit " " \fIFILE\fR
Save VTTY buffer to file on command exit.

.TP
.BR \-K ", " \-\-send\-keys " " \fIKEYS\fR
Send keystrokes after command starts.

.TP
.BR \-\-no\-log
Suppress activity logging (spawning, stopping, resizing). Overrides \-\-log.

.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Alias for \-\-no\-log. Suppress all non-error logging output. Overrides \-\-log.

.TP
.BR \-\-handle\-sigwinch
Resize the VTTY when the terminal where vrc is running is resized. By default VTTY dimensions are fixed at spawn time; with this flag, SIGWINCH events resize all VTTY buffers and PTYs.

.TP
.BR \-\-on\-exit " " \fICMD\fR
Run command on clean exit.

.TP
.BR \-\-on\-error " " \fICMD\fR
Run command on non-zero exit.

.TP
.BR \-\-exit\-timeout " " \fISECS\fR
Seconds before force-killing (default: 10).

.SH FILES

.TP
.BR ~/.local/share/vrc/instances/ " " \fI{pid}.json\fR
Per-instance PID files.

.TP
.BR ~/.local/share/vrc/control\-{pid}.sock
UDS control socket for each instance.

.TP
.BR ~/.config/vrc/config.yaml " " or " " \fIconfig.toml
User configuration file.

.TP
.BR ./vrc.yaml " " or " " \fIvrc.toml
Local configuration file (overrides user config).

.SH EXAMPLES

.PP
Run a command with local terminal display:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrc \-\-display htop\fR
.fi
.RE

.PP
Run a command in the background:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrc \-\-daemon cargo build \-\-release\fR
.fi
.RE

.PP
Send keystrokes to a running command:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrc keys 12345 ctrl-c\fR
.fi
.RE

.PP
View the output of a detached command:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrc cat 12345 | grep "ERROR"\fR
.fi
.RE

.PP
Spawn a new command in a running instance:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrc spawn-in 12345 vim /path/to/file.rs\fR
.fi
.RE

.PP
List all running instances:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrc list\fR
.fi
.RE

.PP
Generate shell completions:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrc completions bash > /etc/bash_completion.d/vrc\fR
.fi
.RE

